  <running_head>Philosoph. Naturalis.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>RE-</catchword>
    <signature>S</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Sed neutra sententia probè collimat in</l>
    <l n="2">punctum. Non prima, ideo enim infinita</l>
    <l n="3">concedit puncta, quia pauca nullam</l>
    <l n="4">facerent extensionem. Contra tamen,</l>
    <l n="5">&amp; rogo: cur v. gr. centum puncta</l>
    <l n="6">non darent extensum? Respondent, quia</l>
    <l n="7">inuicem penetrarentur. Si hoc verum</l>
    <l n="8">est, igitur &amp; infinita penetrabuntur.</l>
    <l n="9">Probo sic. Centesimum v. g. punctum</l>
    <l n="10">etiamsi octo, &amp; nonaginta intermedia</l>
    <l n="11">sint, penetratur cum primo; ergo pe-</l>
    <l n="12">netrabit, quamuis &amp; alia innumera</l>
    <l n="13">interponantur.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Secunda quoque opinio de punctis</l>
    <l n="15">inflatis omnino difflanda est, quippe</l>
    <l n="16">ventosa magis, quàm solida. Quomodo</l>
    <l n="17">enim indiuisibile per modum ex-</l>
    <l n="18">tensum ac diuisibilem vbicari potest?</l>
    <l n="19">alioquin deber concedi, extensum ali-</l>
    <l n="20">quid in inextenso esse receptum. Deinde</l>
    <l n="21">modus, quem habet Angelus occu-</l>
    <l n="22">pandi locum diuisibilem, &amp; extensum,</l>
    <l n="23">conuenit illi ratione spiritualitatis, &amp;</l>
    <l n="24">replicationis eidem naturaliter debitæ:</l>
    <l n="25">sed punctum est materiale, neque vi</l>
    <l n="26">suæ naturæ potest vnquam replicari,</l>
    <l n="27">ergo ad locum diuisibilem coex-</l>
    <l n="28">tendi nequit.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">Dicendum igi-</l>
    <l n="30">tur est, continuum solis</l>
    <l n="31">punctis mathemati-</l>
    <l n="32">cis, &amp; quidem</l>
    <l n="33">finitis com-</l>
    <l n="34">poni.</l>
    <l n="35" type="foot" para="true">Lacunæ in fine.</l>
  </main_text>
